
  riscvsim > demo - a short course on the pipeline, in six lessons

   1  Your first instructions                                     first-steps
      Watch five instructions move through the five stages.
   2  Waiting for memory                                             load-use
      See why an add must wait one cycle for a load.
   3  Skipping the wait                                            forwarding
      Pass a result straight to the next instruction.
   4  Guessing wrong                                                 branches
      A branch guesses, misses, and wrong work is thrown away.
   5  Loops                                                             loops
      Add 1 to 10 and watch the counter count down.
   6  Wide values (RV64)                                          wide-values
      RV64 registers hold 64 bits; see what addw keeps.

  Start: riscvsim demo 1 (or by name: riscvsim demo loops)